Relevant columns and possible usage for calculating “average runs per match in season‑5”  

• match.match_id : key to connect every per‑ball table to the season  
• match.season_id : filter only season 5 (WHERE season_id = 5)  
• ball_by_ball.match_id / over_id / ball_id / innings_no : join keys to batsman_scored  
• ball_by_ball.striker : player_id of the batsman who faced that ball (whose runs we will count)  
• batsman_scored.runs_scored : runs made off that ball by the striker  
• player.player_id : connect to striker so we can pull the name  
• player.player_name : final display field (name of the batsman)  

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Exploratory SQLs (10 different SELECTs, each limited to 20)  
--------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
--1) Description: See which seasons exist in the data set
SELECT DISTINCT season_id
FROM match
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--2) Description: List a few matches that belong to season‑5
SELECT match_id,
       match_date,
       team_1,
       team_2
FROM match
WHERE season_id = 5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--3) Description: Return a sample of balls from one season‑5 match (shows striker & runs)
SELECT b.match_id,
       b.over_id,
       b.ball_id,
       b.striker,
       s.runs_scored
FROM ball_by_ball AS b
JOIN batsman_scored AS s
      ON b.match_id   = s.match_id
     AND b.over_id    = s.over_id
     AND b.ball_id    = s.ball_id
     AND b.innings_no = s.innings_no
WHERE b.match_id IN (SELECT match_id FROM match WHERE season_id = 5)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--4) Description: Distinct player_ids (strikers) who batted in season‑5
SELECT DISTINCT b.striker AS player_id
FROM ball_by_ball AS b
JOIN match            AS m ON m.match_id = b.match_id
WHERE m.season_id = 5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--5) Description: Runs made by each player in a single match (season‑5)
SELECT b.match_id,
       b.striker     AS player_id,
       SUM(s.runs_scored) AS runs_in_match
FROM ball_by_ball AS b
JOIN batsman_scored AS s
      ON b.match_id   = s.match_id
     AND b.over_id    = s.over_id
     AND b.ball_id    = s.ball_id
     AND b.innings_no = s.innings_no
JOIN match AS m ON m.match_id = b.match_id
WHERE m.season_id = 5
GROUP BY b.match_id,
         b.striker
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--6) Description: Number of distinct season‑5 matches each player appeared in
SELECT b.striker          AS player_id,
       COUNT(DISTINCT b.match_id) AS matches_played
FROM ball_by_ball AS b
JOIN match AS m ON m.match_id = b.match_id
WHERE m.season_id = 5
GROUP BY b.striker
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--7) Description: Total runs per player in season‑5
SELECT b.striker AS player_id,
       SUM(s.runs_scored) AS total_runs
FROM ball_by_ball AS b
JOIN batsman_scored AS s
      ON b.match_id   = s.match_id
     AND b.over_id    = s.over_id
     AND b.ball_id    = s.ball_id
     AND b.innings_no = s.innings_no
JOIN match AS m ON m.match_id = b.match_id
WHERE m.season_id = 5
GROUP BY b.striker
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--8) Description: Average runs per match for each player (season‑5)
SELECT player_id,
       total_runs * 1.0 / matches_played AS avg_runs_per_match
FROM (
    SELECT b.striker AS player_id,
           SUM(s.runs_scored)                          AS total_runs,
           COUNT(DISTINCT b.match_id)                  AS matches_played
    FROM ball_by_ball AS b
    JOIN batsman_scored AS s
          ON b.match_id   = s.match_id
         AND b.over_id    = s.over_id
         AND b.ball_id    = s.ball_id
         AND b.innings_no = s.innings_no
    JOIN match AS m ON m.match_id = b.match_id
    WHERE m.season_id = 5
    GROUP BY b.striker
) sub
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--9) Description: Join the previous result to player table and rank by average (top‑10)
SELECT p.player_name,
       sub.avg_runs_per_match
FROM (
    SELECT b.striker AS player_id,
           SUM(s.runs_scored)                         AS total_runs,
           COUNT(DISTINCT b.match_id)                 AS matches_played,
           SUM(s.runs_scored)*1.0 / COUNT(DISTINCT b.match_id) AS avg_runs_per_match
    FROM ball_by_ball AS b
    JOIN batsman_scored AS s
          ON b.match_id   = s.match_id
         AND b.over_id    = s.over_id
         AND b.ball_id    = s.ball_id
         AND b.innings_no = s.innings_no
    JOIN match AS m ON m.match_id = b.match_id
    WHERE m.season_id = 5
    GROUP BY b.striker
) sub
JOIN player AS p ON p.player_id = sub.player_id
ORDER BY sub.avg_runs_per_match DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

```sql
--10) Description: Final answer – names of top 5 players with highest average runs per match in season‑5
SELECT p.player_name                              AS player,
       ROUND(sub.avg_runs_per_match, 2)           AS batting_average
FROM (
    SELECT b.striker AS player_id,
           SUM(s.runs_scored)*1.0 / COUNT(DISTINCT b.match_id) AS avg_runs_per_match
    FROM ball_by_ball AS b
    JOIN batsman_scored AS s
          ON b.match_id   = s.match_id
         AND b.over_id    = s.over_id
         AND b.ball_id    = s.ball_id
         AND b.innings_no = s.innings_no
    JOIN match AS m ON m.match_id = b.match_id
    WHERE m.season_id = 5
    GROUP BY b.striker
) sub
JOIN player AS p ON p.player_id = sub.player_id
ORDER BY sub.avg_runs_per_match DESC
LIMIT 5;
```
